## Unicode Character Database — `src/casefold.zig`

`src/casefold.zig` is the simple case-folding relation of Unicode 15.0.0
(`CaseFolding.txt`, status C and S entries), as Go 1.26's
`unicode.SimpleFold` answers it for every code point; it is generated by
`tools/go_casefold` and compiled into the module (it is what `(?i)` matches
by). It is a TRANSFORMED form of the data, not a copy of the file: the
relation is re-encoded as 366 runs of orbit successors (`lo`, `hi`, `delta` or
alternating pairs). The Unicode License v3 permits modification; the notice
below is reproduced because its clause (a) asks that it appear with all copies
of the Data Files.

## Unicode Character Database — `src/unicode_tables.zig`

`src/unicode_tables.zig` is the General_Category property (`UnicodeData.txt`)
and the Script property (`Scripts.txt`) of Unicode 15.0.0, with the long
category aliases (`PropertyValueAliases.txt`), as Go 1.26's `unicode`
package answers them for every code point; it is generated by
`tools/go_unicode` and compiled into the module (it is what `\p{…}`
matches by). It is a TRANSFORMED form of the data, not a copy of the files:
each two-letter category and each script is re-encoded as code-point ranges
in LEB128 varints, and every other name as a list of those tables. The same
licence and notice apply.

